      "id": "seg:paragraph:overview:0011:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:overview:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "You can add an `OrthographicCameraComponent` to an entity’s component set, and orient that entity so that it looks at a specific target using `Entity/look(at:from:upVector:relativeTo:)`.",
      "normalizedSource": "You can add an `OrthographicCameraComponent` to an entity’s component set, and orient that entity so that it looks at a specific target using `Entity/look(at:from:upVector:relativeTo:)`.",
      "sourceHash": "ab1d64ecb5d64adf212be531989df5e4ee30187433c72c8f9a504364ddf8f2be",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "![A screenshot of three cubes, one behind the other, rendered with a orthographic camera. The cubes appear the same size, regardless of their distance.](https://docs-assets.developer.apple.com/published/6a06251fd3a6fe3a7dca37a87da85cc4/orthocamera-orthographic-cubes.png)",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\n// Create an entity to hold the camera component.\nlet cameraEntity = Entity()\n\n// Create an orthographic camera component and add it to the camera entity.\ncameraEntity.components.set(OrthographicCameraComponent())\n\n// Set the entity's position and orientation to look at the subject.\nlet cameraPosition: SIMD3<Float> = [0, 1, 3]\n\n// The subject in this case is the origin.\nlet target: SIMD3<Float> = .zero\ncameraEntity.look(at: target, from: cameraPosition, relativeTo: nil)\n\n// Add the camera entity to your scene.\ncontent.add(cameraEntity)\n```",
      "documentTitle": "OrthographicCameraComponent",
      "framework": "RealityKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:overview:0012:0001",
      "blockId": "code:overview:0012",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\n// Create an entity to hold the camera component.\nlet cameraEntity = Entity()\n\n// Create an orthographic camera component and add it to the camera entity.\ncameraEntity.components.set(OrthographicCameraComponent())\n\n// Set the entity's position and orientation to look at the subject.\nlet cameraPosition: SIMD3<Float> = [0, 1, 3]\n\n// The subject in this case is the origin.\nlet target: SIMD3<Float> = .zero\ncameraEntity.look(at: target, from: cameraPosition, relativeTo: nil)\n\n// Add the camera entity to your scene.\ncontent.add(cameraEntity)\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift // Create an entity to hold the camera component. let cameraEntity = Entity() // Create an orthographic camera component and add it to the camera entity. cameraEntity.components.set(OrthographicCameraComponent()) // Set the entity's position and orientation to look at the subject. let cameraPosition: SIMD3<Float> = [0, 1, 3] // The subject in this case is the origin. let target: SIMD3<Float> = .zero cameraEntity.look(at: target, from: cameraPosition, relativeTo: nil) // Add the camera entity to your scene. content.add(cameraEntity) ```",
      "sourceHash": "4b1ccd6418260195064ecbdf837727dda6373dd650b8d61473f814350b2c5a94",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "You can add an `OrthographicCameraComponent` to an entity’s component set, and orient that entity so that it looks at a specific target using `Entity/look(at:from:upVector:relativeTo:)`.",
      "contextAfter": "In AR scenarios, the system provides the camera automatically; however, in non-AR scenarios, the app needs to set the camera.",
      "documentTitle": "OrthographicCameraComponent",
      "framework": "RealityKit",
      "ko": "```swift\n// Create an entity to hold the camera component.\nlet cameraEntity = Entity()\n\n// Create an orthographic camera component and add it to the camera entity.\ncameraEntity.components.set(OrthographicCameraComponent())\n\n// Set the entity's position and orientation to look at the subject.\nlet cameraPosition: SIMD3<Float> = [0, 1, 3]\n\n// The subject in this case is the origin.\nlet target: SIMD3<Float> = .zero\ncameraEntity.look(at: target, from: cameraPosition, relativeTo: nil)\n\n// Add the camera entity to your scene.\ncontent.add(cameraEntity)\n```",
      "status": "preserved",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": true
